# FinTRK Admin architecture

Port **3005** (`https://local.admin.fintrk.io:3005`). User app is `FinTRK/` on **3004**.

## Stack

| Piece | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| DB | Neon Postgres (`DATABASE_URL`) — same as user app |
| Auth | Clerk + `ADMIN_EMAILS` allow-list (`lib/auth-admin.ts`) |
| Encryption | Break-the-glass sessions (`lib/decryption-session.ts`); key `FINTRK_ENCRYPTION_KEY` |

## Modules (must stay complete)

Overview · Users (Pro grant/revoke, hard delete) · Messages · Data catalog · Tables DataTable · Crons · Errors · Security (decrypt / audit / secrets / vendors / DRP)

## Domain notes

- FinTRK is **subscription Pro** (Stripe), not credits.
- User-owned rows use `user_id` (Clerk id). Cascade deletes must follow FK order (transactions → statements → accounts → …).
- Encrypted tables decrypt only with an active admin decryption session.
- Cron registry paths live in `lib/cron-registry.ts` and must match user-app `/api/cron/*` routes.

## Do not

- Point admin at a different database than the user app.
- Ship table decrypt without a reason-logged session.
- Remove Overview / Users / DataTable / Security when extending features.
